{{#if (has "deployment" "sst")}}

### Delivery of links on Lambda

The links the project sends through `deliverLink` (`packages/auth/src/link-delivery.ts`) only go to the server logs until a mailer is plugged in, and they leave from `after()`. On SST, Next.js runs through OpenNext on Lambda, which freezes the process when the handler returns, so OpenNext keeps the invocation alive for `after()` work: it hands the task to the `waitUntil` of its streaming Lambda wrapper, which sends the response first, and otherwise awaits every `after()` task before the handler returns (`awaitAllDetachedPromise` in `@opennextjs/aws`, `utils/promise.js`), so no delivery is lost. With the second, the response leaves only once the delivery is done: once a real mailer is plugged in, on an email change a free address answers later than a taken one (Better Auth sends nothing for a taken one), by the time the mailer takes{{#if passwordReset}}, and a password reset is the other way round: an address that has an account answers later than one that has not (nothing is sent for it){{/if}}. A mailer that answers in milliseconds narrows the gap; handing the link to a queue (SQS, ...) instead of sending it closes it.
{{/if}}
